# NestedText v3 - dtds/ per-folder DETAIL pass (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/dtds/ - 12 files, 25.2 KB.
# Completes the office+dtds+daisy trio beside office-dtds-daisy.nt.

folder-shape:
    wire-protocols: presence, watcherinfo, rlmi, mscml, pocsettings, reginfo, xcap-caps, xcap-error (telecom session and capability grammars)
    feeds: rss, itunes (podcast extension), smil (timed media)
    meta: dc (Dublin Core)

protocol-vs-document:
    > Every file here grammars a wire exchange or a feed, not a document:
    > presence and watcherinfo carry session state, xcap-caps negotiates
    > capability, rss carries items. No modules, no drivers, no catalogs;
    > twelve single-purpose grammars averaging 2 KB, the floor below which
    > the loose files' 287-byte minimum is the only smaller grammar.

release-binding:
    > Stream 9 (generation): single-purpose files need no generation
    > discipline; the triple ships for artifacts with more than one
    > consumer, and these twelve have exactly one each.
    > Stream 17 (fixtures): the smallest multi-file battery for sweeps
    > beside the loose ten.
